    "explanation": "Both parties: this case is decided on the platform's own telemetry, and the driver's no-show fee stands.\n\nArrival and termination. The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 18:44:30 and the GPS trace (83 fixes, 100% coverage, no sampling gap, maximum gap 0 s) places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius on 40 qualifying fixes — far more than the three consecutive in-radius fixes POL-NS-02 requires — so arrival and POL-NS-01 limbs (a) and (b) are met. No boarding is recorded, and the driver terminated the trip at 18:52:45 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell had elapsed, so limb (d) is met.\n\nThe dwell the rider contests. The rider is right that the trace shows two separate in-geofence runs — 170 s (18:44:45–18:47:35) and 185 s (18:49:35–18:52:40) — and that neither run alone reaches 300 s. But POL-NS-06(i) expressly permits separate in-geofence intervals within a single pickup attempt to be summed where a KERB_RESTRICTION advisory covers the pickup road and the waiting window and the driver never travelled more than 300 m from the pin. Every condition is met here: LTA advisory ADV-20260807-014 is a bus-lane/kerb restriction in force 17:00–20:00 whose geometry covers the Orchard Turn pickup road, holding position there was not lawfully possible (the driver was moved on by the marshal at about 18:47, and his own chat message at 18:47:50 records it), and his furthest point between the runs was 179 m, inside the 300 m leash. The effective dwell is therefore 355 s against the 300 s minimum — a surplus of 55 s — so limb (c) holds and POL-NS-06's refund condition is not triggered. I answer the rider's contrary submission directly: the summation is a rule about how the dwell limb is measured, and it is what makes the driver's time at the kerb count.\n\nThe rider's other routes. POL-NS-04 does not exonerate her: the driver replied to her 18:46:20 message at 18:47:50, within the 120-second window, so limb (b) fails, and her device shows no qualifying fix inside the 150 m rider-presence radius, sitting 691–717 m from the pin throughout the waiting window, so limb (c) fails too. Her reading of POL-NS-06 ('whether or not the rider was present') is correct in itself but does not help her, because the clause is never reached. There is no false arrival marker under POL-NS-05: the greatest distance from the pin anywhere in the waiting window is the 179 m excursion, well under 300 m, and the first qualifying in-geofence fix follows the marker by 15 seconds. POL-NS-03 does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, and the trip records 1 registered pickup point, so the pin-ambiguity goodwill is unavailable.\n\nThe money. The SGD 4.00 charged reconciles with the fee schedule: the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) are a tie, and the greater is SGD 4.00, matching the cancellation_fee and total_charged lines, so there is no fare-integrity defect. Under POL-NS-07 the driver is compensated at 80% of the fee: SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00, with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform fee. The anti-farming check does not trip — 2 no-show terminations in 30 days is below 4, and 2 ÷ 118 completed trips is 0.017, below 0.08 — so compensation is paid and not withheld. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is met (confidence is above the 0.70 floor, the trace and trip record do not contradict each other on arrival or dwell, the same-pair dispute counters are 0, the anti-farming check is clear, and no deciding artifact is impaired), and no clause produces a referral. No admissibility impairment was flagged on any artifact this ruling relies on. The rider's SGD 4.00 charge stands, and SGD 3.20 moves to the driver."
